(text "USB-C 5 V in (power only, 5.1k CC: a 5 V 3 A supply gives up to 3 A), straight to both FFCs" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 16.51 19.05 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3281e39b-4cce-5b80-8c47-e77be8829997"))
(text "A reset is an unplug: there is no switching here. Each SB1 draws up to ~1 A." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22.86 132.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "92bf78b1-0f3d-5d99-acfe-bad5f00e512c"))
(text "FFC links: J2 to SB1-A, J3 to SB1-B, both to SB1 J7; both reversed, pad n = wire 21 - n" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 217.17 19.05 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e32c3bf6-e4c4-5a09-a666-62ef3a6c5728"))
(text "TXO = radar out (to the adapter RXD), RXI = radar in (from the adapter TXD). 3.3 V logic." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 220.98 132.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "43989ed4-a400-5be1-9e26-12581e86e4dc"))
(text "Radar UARTs to four CP2102 USB-TTL sticks, plugged into right-angle sockets (3V3 / TXD / RXD / GND / 5V; 3V3 and 5V not connected)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 16.51 156.21 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3a93ef3d-4d0e-5c71-b5c8-680e7b0495f4"))
(text "1k in series with each adapter TXD (R8-R11, John 10/31): a powered adapter can no longer hold an unpowered radar up through its RX clamp." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22.86 279.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "5368cf1b-ed09-54a8-9fd3-0b1964d14819"))
(text "CP2102 standard baud table includes 256000 (actual 255319, -0.27 %), so it runs the LD2450." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22.86 271.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "28236ac6-ca43-5b77-b9bf-24a22a0a8d52"))
(text "I2C to an MCP2221A per SB1 (no mux), mic and status headers, mounting" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 217.17 156.21 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "35247b58-4dc5-5ce4-b999-a73c50ab5563"))
(text "The I2C, mic and status lines are on SB1's side of 100 ohm / 33 ohm series resistors; nothing to add here." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 220.98 279.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "71466fc9-719e-5d78-8cd2-4c49d0dd0ae5"))
